{
  "version": 1,
  "commands": [
    {
      "name": "setup-daily-news",
      "description": "Set up the daily AI briefing stack (deps, env vars, Vercel KV, cron).",
      "prompt": [
        "You are helping the user initialize the existing SvelteKit project `daily-news` so it is ready to run the daily AI briefing stack that is already wired into the repo.",
        "",
        "Project facts:",
        "- It is a SvelteKit app configured with the Vercel adapter (see `svelte.config.js`).",
        "- `src/routes/+page.server.ts` reads from a KV-backed Redis client in `src/lib/server/redis.ts` and expects a `daily_cache` key.",
        "- `src/routes/api/cron/+server.ts` calls the Gemini API via `@google/genai`, writes a `daily_cache` payload into Redis, and is protected by a `CRON_SECRET` bearer token.",
        "- `vercel.json` defines a daily cron hitting `/api/cron` at midnight.",
        "- `package.json` already includes `@google/genai`, `@upstash/redis`, `@sveltejs/adapter-vercel`, and `@vercel/analytics`.",
        "",
        "When this command is invoked in this repo, do ALL of the following for the user, step by step:",
        "",
        "1) Verify and install dependencies",
        "- Detect whether `package-lock.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, or `yarn.lock` is present and pick npm / pnpm / yarn accordingly (prefer npm if unsure).",
        "- If node modules are missing or the user agrees, run the appropriate install command (e.g. `npm install`).",
        "- Confirm that the key runtime deps exist in `package.json`: `@google/genai`, `@upstash/redis`, `@sveltejs/adapter-vercel`, `@vercel/analytics`. If any are missing, add them and re-run install.",
        "",
        "2) Set up local environment variables",
        "- If a `.env.local` file does not exist at the project root, create it.",
        "- Ensure it contains the following keys (append them if missing, but never overwrite existing values):",
        "  - `GOOGLE_API_KEY=` (leave value blank and explain the user must paste a key from Google AI Studio).",
        "  - `KV_REST_API_URL=` (blank placeholder for the Vercel KV / Upstash REST URL).",
        "  - `KV_REST_API_TOKEN=` (blank placeholder for the Vercel KV / Upstash REST token).",
        "  - `CRON_SECRET=` (generate a strong random string locally and prefill it if possible; otherwise, suggest a value to the user).",
        "- Briefly explain what each variable is used for and that `.env.local` should not be committed.",
        "",
        "3) Guide the user through Vercel KV setup",
        "- Explain, in concise steps, how to create a Vercel KV (Upstash Redis) instance in the Vercel dashboard and how to copy the REST URL/token values.",
        "- Map those dashboard values explicitly to `KV_REST_API_URL` and `KV_REST_API_TOKEN` in `.env.local` and in Vercel project environment variables.",
        "",
        "4) Wire up the cron secret on Vercel",
        "- Ensure the same `CRON_SECRET` value is present both locally and in the Vercel project environment variables.",
        "- Point out that Vercel's cron job will call `/api/cron` with an `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` header, matching the check in `src/routes/api/cron/+server.ts`.",
        "",
        "5) Optional: enable basic analytics",
        "- If `@vercel/analytics` is installed, show the user (or offer to add) the minimal `+layout.svelte` injection using `inject` from `@vercel/analytics`, only in production.",
        "",
        "6) Final verification and local run",
        "- Run the typecheck (`npm run check`) if available.",
        "- Start the dev server (`npm run dev`) or show the exact command so the user can run it.",
        "- Provide a short checklist so the user can verify everything is working:",
        "  - The home page renders (even if KV is not yet populated).",
        "  - Hitting `/api/cron` manually with the correct `CRON_SECRET` returns `Daily update complete.`.",
        "  - After the cron or manual hit, the home page shows AI-generated content instead of the placeholder message.",
        "",
        "Throughout:",
        "- Be concise and action-oriented.",
        "- Prefer actually running commands and editing files in this repo (using the Cursor tools) rather than only describing what to do.",
        "- Do not re-architect the app; assume the existing SvelteKit + KV + cron + Gemini design is intentional.",
        "- If something is already set up (dependencies installed, env file present, etc.), acknowledge it briefly and skip redundant work."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

